{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Spatial lab / colour family",
  "_doc": "Colour recipes for /spatial-lab (Palle 2026-10-27: 'we should use a system like this for fast color test', 'one lab'). A recipe is an existing artifact scene plus parameters. Each parameter is either an exported property (`export`) or a config word stamped as a config_<key> meta before the artifact enters the tree (`config`), exactly as a map token or a Void record would carry it. The truth is a native Godot picture on the Mobile renderer (the Quest's), rendered by tools/colour_bench.py + commons/testing/colour_bench.gd; the browser shows that picture, not a three.js imitation. An `oracle` names how the receipt checks pixels against expected colours; a recipe without one is pictures only, and the receipt says so. Recipes are listed in the order of the Void's colour floors (29-36); every enum parameter is derived from the artifact's own @export_enum (values and default), never transcribed.",
  "renderer": "mobile",
  "recipes": [
    {
      "id": "array_lattice",
      "label": "Array · Lattice (grid_3d_4x4x4) / occupancy rule",
      "scene": "res://algorithms/arrays/grid_3d_4x4x4.tscn",
      "watch": [
        "algorithms/arrays/grid_3d_4x4x4.gd",
        "commons/artifacts/regularity/address_rules.gd",
        "commons/modular/mod_mesh.gd"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "occupancy": {
          "kind": "config",
          "type": "enum",
          "values": [
            "none",
            "sum",
            "difference",
            "columns",
            "rows",
            "knight",
            "linear",
            "product",
            "squares",
            "gcd",
            "pascal",
            "xor",
            "and",
            "rings",
            "diamonds",
            "frames",
            "sectors",
            "spiral",
            "primes",
            "collatz",
            "scatter"
          ],
          "default": "none",
          "label": "Occupancy (#occupancy:<rule>; none = the lattice as it always was)"
        }
      },
      "views": [
        "front",
        "oblique",
        "eye"
      ],
      "oracle": null,
      "note": "The hall's own lattice, natively. Where the rule gives 0 (with the layer added) the address stands empty: a frame and its label. Pickup cubes are rigid bodies and settle while the picture is taken."
    },
    {
